# Granete backend — example environment.
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in real values. NEVER commit `.env.local`.
# `.env*` is gitignored; this `.env.example` is tracked on purpose.
#
# Setup:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#   # edita .env.local: JWT_SECRET="$(openssl rand -base64 48)"
#
# #460 / ADR-0007 — token issuer y keyring (opcionales):
# #   JWT_ISSUER: issuer de los tokens ver5 (default "granete-api").
# #   JWT_KEYRING: JSON {"active_kid":"k1","keys":{"k1":"...","k0":"..."}}
# #   para rotación sin downtime. Sin JWT_KEYRING, JWT_SECRET se registra
# #   bajo el kid "legacy" (los tokens ver4 validan contra esa entrada).
# #   Al rotar a un keyring, registrá el JWT_SECRET anterior bajo kid "legacy"
# #   o los tokens ver4 vigentes dejan de validar (fail-closed).
#   cd backend-go && ./dev.sh        # arranca el server Go con estas vars

# --- Backend Go ---
PORT=8080

# --- Database ---
# Local dev default points to the docker-compose Postgres on :5445.
# Production MUST set its own DSN with TLS, e.g. sslmode=require (or verify-full).
# The Go process serves plain HTTP; terminate TLS/HTTPS + HSTS at a reverse proxy.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://granete_app:granete_app@localhost:5445/muebles?sslmode=disable
MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5445/muebles?sslmode=disable

# --- Security: JWT (REQUIRED) ---
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 48
# Must be >= 32 bytes. The server refuses to boot if missing or too short.
JWT_SECRET=
# Dedicated HMAC pepper for opaque refresh credential lookup. Generate
# independently from JWT_SECRET: openssl rand -base64 48
REFRESH_TOKEN_PEPPER=
# #460 SEC-3 — dedicated signing key for resource-scoped media read grants
# (media_read). Independent from JWT_SECRET/JWT_KEYRING/REFRESH_TOKEN_PEPPER:
# a media grant can never validate as a session credential and vice versa.
# Must be >= 32 bytes; the server refuses to boot if missing or too short.
MEDIA_SIGNING_KEY=

# --- Security: CORS allowlist ---
# Comma-separated list of allowed origins. Never use "*" in production.
# Defaults to the Vite dev/preview servers if unset.
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:4173

# --- Security: Web refresh cookie (#460 SEC-4A / ADR-0007 §9) ---
# GRANETE_ENV signals the deployment shape: "production" or "development"
# (default). docker-compose.prod.yml pins GRANETE_ENV=production (not
# overridable via .env).
# WEB_REFRESH_COOKIE_SECURE controls the Secure attribute of the HttpOnly
# granete_web_refresh cookie: "auto" (default; Secure unless every CORS origin
# is loopback HTTP, i.e. the local dev/gate shape), "true", or "false".
# Under GRANETE_ENV=production any resolution to Secure=false makes the
# server refuse to boot — production can never ship an insecure refresh cookie.
#GRANETE_ENV=development
#WEB_REFRESH_COOKIE_SECURE=auto

# --- Security: rate limiting on /api/auth/login and /api/auth/register ---
# Sustained requests/second and max burst per client IP.
RATE_LIMIT_RPS=0.2
RATE_LIMIT_BURST=5

# --- Catalog media storage ---
# Where uploaded catalog images (materials / hardware / modules) live on disk.
# Default is an absolute path OUTSIDE the repo (~/.muebles-media) so uploads
# survive `git clean`, re-clones and machine changes. Override only if you need
# a different location; absolute or relative both work. The server logs the
# resolved path on boot. Cleanup of dangling URLs after data loss:
#   cd backend-go && ./dev.sh admin clean-media [--apply]
# MEDIA_DIR=

# --- Frontend (Vite, apps/web) ---
# Overrides DEFAULT_API_BASE in session.ts. Vite loads .env.local automatically.
VITE_API_BASE=http://localhost:8080/api

# --- Admin CLI (cmd/admin) ---
# Only used by `./dev.sh admin create|reset-password` in non-interactive
# mode (e.g. CI). In interactive mode the password is prompted without echo.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=
